! mcp_bootstrap_p167.strap -- THE DENSITY AND MODE CHANGE PSEUDO-OPS:
! the six tape-attribute entry points RHD, RLD, REVEN, RODD, RECC
! and RNOECC, their two common tails RTAPE and RSFMOD, and the
! all-pseudo-ops exit RALLPS.  Printed page 167,
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.174.
!
! THE HEADER WAS READ, NOT ASSUMED.  The top line prints
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID IN000001
! DIST. OF 3/01    3/01    PAGE NUMBER  167", and the column
! heading row's own right-hand "LOCATION" field is BLANK --
! correctly so, because line 1 is an asterisk banner that compiles
! nothing (docs/transcription_workflow.md 1).  A blank there is not
! a zero and not a refutation of anything; see THE JOIN BACKWARD.
!
! THE CARD ID RESTARTS AT IN000001 ON THIS PAGE.  Printed p.166
! runs in the IE deck; p.167 line 1 is card IN000001 and line 37 is
! IN000035.  A new card deck does NOT reset the location counter --
! line 4's printed "SLC,$" is the proof, see THE JOIN BACKWARD.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIRTY-SEVEN PRINTED LINES: three asterisk banners (1-3), one
! "SLC,$" that emits nothing (line 4), and THIRTY-THREE located
! instructions (lines 5-37) -- twenty-nine half words and four full
! words.  No DD, no SYN, no VF, no reservation, no comment card and
! no comment text in the right-hand column.  Blank paper from line
! 38 to the foot of the form.
!
! THIS IS THE $DENSITY / $MODE PSEUDO-OP SERVICE.  Each entry point
! loads a two-bit code into index 5, saves it in $R, and stores it
! into the file area table through index $13:
!
!   RHD     (line  5)  LVI,5,1.0   -> SFDEN  = 01  High density
!   RLD     (line  7)  LVI,5,3.0   -> SFDEN  = 11  Low density
!   REVEN   (line 18)  LVI,5,2.0   -> SFMODE = 10  Even parity
!   RODD    (line 20)  LVI,5,3.0   -> SFMODE = 11  Odd parity
!   RECC    (line 24)  LVI,5,1.0   -> SFMODE = 01  Odd parity, ECC
!   RNOECC  (line 28)  LVI,5,3.0   -> SFMODE = 11  Odd parity, no ECC
!
! C22-6728-1 (MCP System Analysis Guide) PRINTED p.271, Appendix A,
! "Symbolic I-O Control Tables", prints the SFDEN codes outright --
!
!     2.27 - 2.28  SFDEN   00 - Null   01 - High
!                          10 - Illegal   11 - Low
!
! -- which is the page's own lines 5 and 7 character for character,
! and its printed p.273 gives 2.48 - 2.49 SFMODE as "the mode
! specified on the IOD card".  C22-6678-1 (MCP Reference Manual)
! PRINTED p.10 prints the IOD card's two fields:
!
!     The mode field ... must be one of the following:
!         ODD   Odd parity, no ECC
!         EVEN  Even parity
!         ECC   Odd parity, ECC
!     The density field ... must contain one of the following:
!         HD    High density
!         LD    Low density
!
! THAT IS WHAT NAMES THE SIX ENTRY POINTS, and it is the whole of
! the glyph argument for RHD, RLD, RODD, RECC and RNOECC -- see
! GLYPHS below.  It also explains why RODD and RNOECC both load 3:
! "no ECC" IS odd parity, so the two requests reach the same code.
!
! Between the entry points and the store sit two shared tails:
!
!   RTAPE  (lines 14-17)  the DENSITY tail.  It tests index 4
!          (KVI,4,4.0 ; BZXE,KILEGL -- an illegal request if the
!          unit is not a tape), then LVI,3,13.32 and B,KNI+1.0.
!
!   RSFMOD (lines 32-34)  the MODE tail.  SV,5,$R ;
!          ST(BU,2),SFMODE($13),46 ; B,RTAPE.32 -- it rejoins the
!          density tail one half word in, at line 15.
!
! RALLPS (lines 35-37) is the common exit: V-I,2,.32 ;
! SV,2,STIC ; B,W23K.  Another page branches to it --
! see THE WITNESSES.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- WHAT WAS SETTLED, AND ON WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE OPENS ROUND GLYPHS HARDER THAN ANY PAGE IN THE BLOCK.
! Every LOCATION reads "22C325.CC" for 220325.00 and every leading
! zero of a BINARY OUTPUT octal group reads "COCCC1.13" for
! 000001.13.  All of those are settled outright by the octal-field
! argument (docs/transcription_workflow.md 2b rung 5): a C cannot
! occur in a field that holds octal digits.
!
! THE HEX BYTES ARE WHERE IT MATTERS, AND THIS PAGE SPLITS BOTH WAYS
! INSIDE A SINGLE TWO-CHARACTER BYTE.  It is settled WITHOUT INK, on
! what produced the byte (docs/transcription_workflow.md 2b, "AND
! SETTLE A BYTE ON WHAT PRODUCED IT"): the operation byte of an
! immediate index instruction is FORCED by its mnemonic, and the
! statement column prints the mnemonic unambiguously.  Measured on
! this repository's assembler, varying only the operation:
!
!     KVNI,5,0   ->  000000.13 0C        BZXE,X     ->  220064.32 C0
!     KVI ,5,0   ->  000000.13 04        BXE ,X     ->  220064.32 C2
!     LVI ,5,0   ->  000000.13 01        BZXE,X.32  ->  220064.72 C0
!     LVNI,5,0   ->  000000.13 09
!     V-I ,2,.32 ->  000000.45 0D
!     V+I ,2,.32 ->  000000.45 05
!
! So:
!
! (1) LINE 12 PRINTS "COCCCO.13 CC" AND THE BYTE IS "0C".  KVNI can
!     produce nothing else.  The first character is a dropped 0 and
!     the SECOND IS A REAL C -- the C is KVNI's own operation bit
!     pattern, which is what separates it from KVI's 04 and LVNI's
!     09.  Line 35 is the same shape: "CCCCCO.45 CD" is 0D, and the
!     D (not a worn 0) is what separates V-I from V+I's 05.
!
! (2) LINES 13, 15 AND 26 PRINT "...CC" AND THE BYTE IS "C0" --
!     EXACTLY THE OPPOSITE SPLIT, on the same page, in the same
!     column.  BZXE's byte is C0: a REAL C in the high nibble and a
!     dropped 0 in the low one.  So "CC" is 0C on line 12 and C0 on
!     lines 13, 15 and 26, which is docs/transcription_workflow.md's
!     "INK VARIES PER CHARACTER, NOT PER ROW" in its sharpest form
!     seen so far -- not two rows calling opposite ways, but two
!     characters of ONE BYTE.
!
! (3) LINE 30 IS THE PAGE'S OWN CONTROL and needs no argument at
!     all: "BXE,RSFMOD" prints "22C344.32 C2", a C beside a 2 that
!     nothing could mistake, and C2 is what BXE compiles to.  It
!     fixes BZXE/BXE's high nibble as a real C from inside the page.
!
! (4) PRINTED p.168 LINE 6 CARRIES LINE 35'S CARD AGAIN at
!     220350.40 ("V-I,2,.32", 000000.45) -- a second instance, but
!     on the next page, so it is corroboration for p.168's
!     transcriber and not a witness here.
!
! THE SIX ENTRY-POINT NAMES ARE SETTLED BY THE MANUALS AND NOT BY
! INK, and that is the honest statement of it.  At 1200 dpi this
! drum prints RECC as four characters R, E, and two IDENTICAL open
! rounds, and RNOECC as R, N, and four characters of which the
! 3rd, 5th and 6th are the SAME open round.  O and C are
! indistinguishable here by shape; the discriminator is
! C22-6678-1 printed p.10's list of IOD mode values (ODD / EVEN /
! ECC), which makes line 24 R-ECC and line 28 R-NO-ECC, and
! C22-6728-1 printed p.271's SFDEN table, which makes lines 5 and 7
! R-HD and R-LD.  The same list fixes RODD, whose ink is "RCCD":
! O dropped to C, the first D worn through to C, the second D
! intact.
!
!   >>> AND THERE IS A SECOND PAGE'S CARD FOR FIVE OF THE SIX.
!   >>> No LANDED DECK references any of these names (grepped over
!   >>> all of decks/*.strap: zero hits for RHD, RLD, REVEN, RODD,
!   >>> RECC, RNOECC, RSFMOD and RALLPS; the one RTAPE hit is a
!   >>> comment about the different symbol "S RTAPE").  So
!   >>> check_symbol_spellings.py cannot corroborate them today.
!   >>> BUT A DISPATCH TABLE ON PRINTED pp.178-179 BRANCHES TO ALL
!   >>> SIX IN THIS PAGE'S OWN ORDER, and the volume OCR indexes it
!   >>> (PDF pp.185-186):
!   >>>
!   >>>     220775.00  220325.10 00  B,RHD      (OCR "B,RED")
!   >>>     220775.40  220326.10 00  B,RLD
!   >>>     220776.00  220334.50 00  B,REVEN
!   >>>     220776.40  2203?5.50 00  B,RODD     (OCR "220235.50")
!   >>>     220777.00  220340.10 00  B,RECC
!   >>>     220777.40  220342.10 00  B,RNOECC   (OCR "B,RNGECC")
!   >>>
!   >>> That is a DIFFERENT PAGE's ink, so rule 5 admits it (what
!   >>> printed p.129 got burned for was using page N's own OCR as
!   >>> page N's witness).  Five of the six addresses agree with
!   >>> this deck's symbol table to the half word -- RHD 220325.00,
!   >>> RLD 220326.00, REVEN 220334.40, RECC 220340.00,
!   >>> RNOECC 220342.00 -- and the sixth agrees except for an OCR
!   >>> digit drop.  It also reads "RECC" with the same two
!   >>> characters at the end off a second impression, and reads
!   >>> RNOECC's third character as a G, which among O/C/D/G is
!   >>> evidence for a CLOSED round and therefore for the O.
!   >>> The addresses are the robust part; the names are
!   >>> corroboration, not proof.  If a later page's own render
!   >>> spells one of these differently, THAT page's ink wins over
!   >>> this argument.
!
! RSFMOD (line 32) is read R-S-F-M-O-D, six characters, from the
! field it stores: SFMODE.  RALLPS (line 35) prints six
! unambiguous characters.  RTAPE and REVEN print clean.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN BACKWARD -- line 4 prints the arriving counter
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 4 IS "220325.00  *   SLC,$".  An SLC emits nothing, so its
! printed LOCATION _is_ the counter arriving from printed p.166 --
! IBM's own assembler stating the join (docs/transcription_workflow
! .md, WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE 2).  THIS PAGE THEREFORE BEGINS AT
! 220325.00 AND SAYS SO ITSELF.
!
! THE SURVEY SAID PRINTED p.166 ENDS AT 220302.40 AND THAT IS A
! LOWER BOUND, NOT A DISAGREEMENT.  The volume OCR of PDF p.173
! (printed p.166) carries lines 52-56 past that point, ending
! "56*  220324.40   216242.10 00   B,K SUPP" -- a half word at
! 220324.40 leaves the counter at 220325.00, which is this page's
! line 4 exactly.  That OCR is an INDEX and not a witness (rule 5);
! what makes the join safe here is that p.167's OWN printed SLC,$
! states 220325.00 independently of it.  If p.166's transcriber
! lands a page ending anywhere other than 220325.00, one of the two
! readings is wrong and this row is where to look.
!
! THE PRINTED FORM WAS HANDED TO strap_asm FIRST, as the brief
! requires, AND IT IS NOT REJECTED -- WHICH IS THE PROBLEM.
! Measured: this deck with line 4 written as the printed "SLC,$"
! assembles cleanly and lands RHD at 000040.00, the assembler's own
! starting counter, because a standalone deck has no previous page
! to supply the arriving value.  A bare "SLC,$" here would be a
! silent error, not an error message.
!
! SO THE DECK RESTATES THE ORIGIN HARD as "SLC, (8)220325.0".  THIS
! IS A LABELLED SUBSTITUTION: the printed form is "SLC,$" and the
! deck writes a hard origin.  That throws the witness away inside
! the deck -- a hard SLC cannot disagree with an arriving counter,
! it overrides it -- so the printed value is recorded above, in THE
! PRINTED LISTING and in line 4's own row, and the comparison with
! printed p.166 has to be made BY HAND.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE WITNESSES -- what is checked and what is only asserted
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! CHECKED BY THE PAGE'S OWN BINARY, all 37 half words:
!
!   * SFDEN  at 2.27 and SFMODE at 2.48, to the BIT.  A VFL
!     operand prints its full address, so line 9's "000002.33"
!     checks 0o33 = 27 and lines 22/33's "000002.60" checks
!     0o60 = 48.  These are not half-word-only externals.
!   * The ",46" offset on lines 9, 22 and 33, as "002027.20".
!     Bits 44-50 of that half word are 0101110 = 46.  BUT the
!     offset field is SEVEN BITS AND WRAPS (docs/transcription_
!     workflow.md, WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE 4), so 46 is pinned
!     only mod 128.
!   * CM1111's connective, as "001000.36 F0" on line 10 -- byte
!     for byte what printed p.18 prints six times.
!   * SFILEK's word and half word: line 11's "000007.52" is
!     0o40 (bit 32 of SFILEK's 7.38) + 0o12 (LV with index 5).
!     The bits BELOW 32 are not observable here; 7.38 comes from
!     printed p.101 line 25.
!   * SVER at 0.40, as line 10's "000000.50" -- 0o50 = 40.
!   * Eleven internal forward and backward references, each
!     against this page's own counter: RLD.32 (line 6),
!     RODD.32 (19), RTAPE (23), RNOECC.32 (26), RSFMOD (27, 30),
!     RTAPE.32 (34).  Line 34's "220333.10" is RTAPE + 32 bits
!     rounding into the next word, which checks RTAPE's own
!     half word from the other side.
!
! ASSERTED AND NOT CHECKED BELOW THE HALF WORD (the standard loss):
!
!   * KILEGL  220064.00  printed p.160 line 8's own label row.
!             Lines 13 and 15 are BZXE branches, so bit 18 only.
!   * K NI    220726.40  NOT DEFINED BY ANY LANDED DECK.  Line 17
!             is "B,KNI+1.0" printing 220727.50; a branch's byte
!             carries 0o10, so the target half word is 220727.40
!             and K NI is one word earlier.  The volume OCR of a
!             LATER page prints the defining card --
!             "42*  220726.40  *  000013.47 04   K NI  KVI,3,11.32"
!             -- and a second card there, "B,K NI" at 220726.50.
!             That is an index, not a witness; this deck SYNs
!             220726.40 off ITS OWN printed branch, and the page
!             that prints K NI's label is the authority on both its
!             spelling (which is "K NI", with the space p.167 does
!             not print) and its bit offset.
!   * W23K    220017.40  carried by the pp.123 and 158 decks, one
!             of which prints the defining card
!             "W 23K  LCI,7,(8)40  -FAKE EOP".  Line 37's
!             "220017.50" agrees on bit 18.
!   * STIC    215265.00  printed p.116 line 16's VF card.  Line 36
!             prints "215265.05", whose 0o05 is SV's index-2 bits,
!             so this page observes the word and nothing under it.
!
! A SECOND, INDEPENDENT READING OF THIS PAGE'S OWN ADDRESSES comes
! from the forward references on later pages, which the volume OCR
! indexes: "B,RHD" prints 220325.10 and "B,RALLPS" prints
! 220346.10 -- RHD at 220325.00 and RALLPS at 220346.00, which are
! this page's line 5 and line 35.  Same drum, so it is an index;
! but an ADDRESS is the OCR-robust part of a card and these two
! agree with the deck's counter to the half word.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK -- two rows, counted not eyed
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every LINE number carries an asterisk ("1*", "37*"); that is the
! ordinary column.  TWO rows carry the SECOND asterisk, in its own
! column to the right of the LOCATION value.  Established by dark-
! pixel count in a 110-px-wide window on that column alone at 300
! dpi -- 209 and 205 dark px on exactly two rows, against the 2-4 px
! of a dashed rule everywhere else:
!
!   LINE  4  220325.00   the printed "SLC,$"
!   LINE 24  220340.00   "RECC  LVI,5,1.0", an ENTRY POINT LABEL
!
! docs/listing_typography.md 12 records the mark as open with eight
! things it is not.  THIS PAGE REFUTES NOTHING AND PROPOSES
! NOTHING, deliberately: line 4 is consistent with p.147's dead
! "every SLC,$ row" rule and line 24 is consistent with nothing at
! all, and a pitch of 20 on a 37-line page is consistent with the
! dead pitch reading too.  One observation IS worth passing on
! because it is cheap to kill:
!
!   HYPOTHESIS (weak, offered only so somebody can shoot it): on
!   this page the two marked rows are the FIRST ROW OF A CARD-DECK
!   SECTION and an ENTRY POINT whose predecessor is a branch that
!   does not fall through.  THE PAGE THAT KILLS IT IS printed
!   p.160, whose marked lines 7 and 26 are "B,K ILEGL.32" and
!   "CM0000(BU,1),S SEL($11)" -- neither is a label at all.  So
!   treat it as already dead and do not re-propose it.
!
! Whatever the mark means it changes no assembled bit: both marked
! rows are in the checked set below and both match the printed
! BINARY OUTPUT character for character.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT COULD NOT BE SETTLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (a) THE SIX ENTRY-POINT NAMES REST ON THE MANUALS PLUS ONE OTHER
!     PAGE'S DISPATCH TABLE, NOT ON THIS PAGE'S INK.  See GLYPHS.
!     RECC/RECO and RNOECC/RNOECO/RNDECC are indistinguishable on
!     this drum at 1200 dpi, and the assembler cannot help -- they
!     are labels, not mnemonics.  C22-6678-1 printed p.10's IOD
!     mode list is the evidence, and printed pp.178-179's six
!     branches corroborate it from a second impression.  NEITHER IS
!     THIS PAGE, and no landed deck references the names, so a
!     passing page check still says nothing about them.
!
! (b) K NI's BIT OFFSET IS READ FROM A BRANCH, so only its word and
!     half word are observed.  Worse, its NAME is read from this
!     page's tight "KNI" while the volume OCR of its own defining
!     page spells it "K NI".  STRAP ignores blanks inside a name so
!     the deck is right either way, but a later transcriber of that
!     page should not take "KNI" from here as a reading of the
!     spacing.
!
! (c) THE ",46" OFFSET IS PINNED ONLY MOD 128 by this page's three
!     stores.  46 is what the statement column prints and 46 is
!     what the deck writes; a reader who needs the absolute offset
!     needs a page that prints the field some other way.
!
! (d) WHAT THE ",46" IS AN OFFSET FROM was not established, and the
!     repo says it is NOT a property of the field.  SFDEN is at 2.27
!     of the file area table and SFMODE at 2.48; the guide's Figure
!     148 (printed p.272) does not explain the displacement and no
!     primary source consulted here does.  What the other decks show
!     is that the offset varies by CALL SITE, not by symbol:
!
!       printed p.156 line  5   L(BU,1),SFDEN($13),46     offset 46
!       printed p.155 line 30   C0011(BU,1),SFDEN($13),6  offset  6
!
!     -- the same field through the same index register with two
!     different offsets.  So "every page writes 46" is FALSE and
!     this page's three stores establish only their own 46 (and that
!     only mod 128, per (c)).  The bits are checked; the MEANING is
!     not claimed.
!
! (e) THE RIGHT-HAND COMMENT COLUMN IS EMPTY ON ALL 33 CODE ROWS.
!     That removes the English oracle that settled names on pp.84,
!     85 and 138, and it is why (a) had to go to the manuals.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN FORWARD -- a falsifiable prediction for printed p.168
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Line 37 is a half-word branch at 220347.00, so THE COUNTER LEAVES
! THIS PAGE AT 220347.40.  Three ways to break that:
!
!   1. printed p.168's first LOCATED row should be 220347.40.
!   2. Its heading-row LOCATION field should be BLANK, because
!      p.168 opens with an asterisk banner.  A blank is not a
!      refutation of (1); a NUMBER other than 220347 would be.
!   3. If p.168 prints its own "SLC,$", that row's LOCATION is the
!      arriving counter and must read 220347.40.
!
! And two more, stronger because they name content:
!
!   4. p.168's first located instruction should be labelled K WAIT
!      and should be a full word, "L(BU,1),S OWNER($10),-18", so
!      its SECOND printed row is at 220350.40.
!   5. That second row should be "V-I,2,.32" printing
!      000000.45 0D -- the SAME CARD as this page's line 35, which
!      gives p.168's transcriber a cross-page check on that byte.
!
! The volume OCR of PDF p.175 carries all five, which is why they
! are worth writing down -- and it is an INDEX, not a witness;
! p.168's own render decides it.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS.  Each carries the DATA DESCRIPTION printed on the page
! that DEFINES it, because a connective or VFL operation writing no
! dds takes its length from the symbol and the merged image refuses
! a disagreement.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SFDEN      2.27    printed p.102 line 12 "-IOD DENSITY"; the two
!                    bits are checked by line 9's 000002.33.
SFDEN   SYN(BU,2), 2.27
! SFMODE     2.48    printed p.102 line 13 "-FILE MODE"; checked by
!                    lines 22 and 33's 000002.60.
SFMODE  SYN(BU,2), 2.48
! SFILEK     7.38    printed p.101 line 25 "-FILE COUNT".  Line 11
!                    observes word 7 and bit 32 only.
SFILEK  SYN(BU,12), 7.38
! SVER       0.40    printed p.99 line 32 "-VERIFY FILE STATUS";
!                    checked by line 10's 000000.50.
SVER    SYN(BU,1), 0.40
! KILEGL  220064.0   printed p.160 line 8's label row.  Lines 13 and
!                    15 are branches: bit 18 only.
KILEGL  SYN, (8)220064.0
! K NI    220726.40  NOT defined by any landed deck.  Read off line
!                    17's own printed branch 220727.50 = KNI+1.0;
!                    see THE WITNESSES.  Bit offset below bit 32 is
!                    unobservable here.
KNI     SYN, (8)220726.40
! W23K    220017.40  pp.123/158 decks, "W 23K LCI,7,(8)40 -FAKE EOP".
W23K    SYN, (8)220017.40
! STIC    215265.0   printed p.116 line 16's VF card; STored
!                    Instruction Counter (C22-6728, 75 hits for
!                    STIC and none for STIO).
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0

! THE ORIGIN.  The page prints "SLC,$" on line 4 at 220325.00.
! RESTATED HARD HERE, which asserts it rather than checking it --
! see THE JOIN BACKWARD.
        SLC, (8)220325.0

RHD     LVI,5,1.0                    ! line  5   (density: HD = 01)
        B,RLD.32                     ! line  6
RLD     LVI,5,3.0                    ! line  7   (density: LD = 11)
        SV,5,$R                      ! line  8
        ST(BU,2),SFDEN($13),46       ! line  9
        CM1111(BU,1),SVER($11)       ! line 10
        LV,5,SFILEK($12)             ! line 11
        KVNI,5,0                     ! line 12   (card IN000012, stmt 1)
        BZXE,KILEGL                  ! line 13   (card IN000012, stmt 2)
RTAPE   KVI,4,4.0                    ! line 14   (card IN000013, stmt 1)
        BZXE,KILEGL                  ! line 15   (card IN000013, stmt 2)
        LVI,3,13.32                  ! line 16
        B,KNI+1.0                    ! line 17
REVEN   LVI,5,2.0                    ! line 18   (mode: EVEN = 10)
        B,RODD.32                    ! line 19
RODD    LVI,5,3.0                    ! line 20   (mode: ODD = 11)
        SV,5,$R                      ! line 21
        ST(BU,2),SFMODE($13),46      ! line 22
        B,RTAPE                      ! line 23
RECC    LVI,5,1.0                    ! line 24   (mode: ECC = 01)
        KVI,4,4.0                    ! line 25
        BZXE,RNOECC.32               ! line 26
        B,RSFMOD                     ! line 27
RNOECC  LVI,5,3.0                    ! line 28   (no ECC IS odd parity)
        KVI,4,1.32                   ! line 29
        BXE,RSFMOD                   ! line 30
        KVI,4,2.0                    ! line 31
RSFMOD  SV,5,$R                      ! line 32
        ST(BU,2),SFMODE($13),46      ! line 33
        B,RTAPE.32                   ! line 34
RALLPS  V-I,2,.32                    ! line 35
        SV,2,STIC                    ! line 36
        B,W23K                       ! line 37

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, recorded so the oracle can check it later.
! Transcribed from PDF p.174 at 600 dpi (LOCATION + BINARY OUTPUT
! and NAME + STATEMENT in three bands each) and 1200 dpi for the
! names of lines 24, 28 and 32.  The card-identification column was
! read at 600 dpi: IN000001..IN000035, with IN000012 and IN000013
! each carrying TWO statements -- so 35 cards for 37 lines, nothing
! missing off either end of the page.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  1*                                                      ------------------------------------------------------  IN000001
!   line  2*                                                      ------------DENSITY AND MODE CHANGE PSEUDO-OPS--------  IN000002
